        {"staticObjects":[],"dynamicObjects":[{"objectId":"story_dialogue","position":{"x":140,"y":-28},"objectData":{
            "text":"(Mr. Bennet reaches another crossing and notices a woman wandering around aimlessly):nl:nlMr. Bennet: Hello, m’lady.:nl:nlBeatrice: Are you flirting with me?:nl:nlMr. Bennet: Am I?:nl:nlBeatrice: That’s what all the other men do, I have a husband, mind you.\\Mr. Bennet: (God, the youth these days) No, I have a wife, thank you very much.:nl:nlBeatrice: Is she pretty?:nl:nlMr. Bennet: Not particularly, but we have come to understand each other.:nl:nlBeatrice: I am probably prettier than her. If I were you, I’d choose me, I’m single, you know.\\Mr. Bennet: Listen, I don’t have time for your antics. Have you seen another young lady pass by?:nl:nlBeatrice: (Gasp) You are seeing another lady? I thought you had a wife…:nl:nlMr. Bennet: (God, I despise this girl) No, she is my daughter. Have you seen her?:nl:nlBeatrice: Oh, no, I haven’t seen anyone pass by.\\Mr. Bennet: Are you sure of it?:nl:nlBeatrice: 100% confident.:nl:nlMr. Bennet: And why is that?:nl:nlBeatrice: Because I’m blind!:nl:nlMr. Bennet: That would have been nice to know earlier…:nl:nlBeatrice: I didn’t see it as important.\\Mr. Bennet: (What a waste of time) Well, thank you for your time.:nl:nl(Mr. Bennet wanders off in a random direction after learning absolutely nothing)"
        }}]},

