        {"staticObjects":[],"dynamicObjects":[{"objectId":"story_dialogue","position":{"x":140,"y":-28},"objectData":{
            "text":"(Mr. Bennet approaches the building with Mr. Wickham and Lydia standing out front and punches Wickham in the face):nl:nlMr. Bennet: (At last, I found them…) Wickham you horrible, horrible man. You won’t escape the country, and I’ll make sure of that. Mr. Darcy! Over here!:nl:nlMr. Darcy (to Mr. Wickham): How much do you need?\\Mr. Wickham (Shocked): (What is going on…) 1400£ will cover all of my debts I suppose.:nl:nlMr. Darcy: (This is pocket change to me) Then this shall be enough for the wedding and for your debts. And here is 1000£ which is designated for you, Lydia.:nl:nlMr. Bennet (to himself): He’s paying them for this marriage that does not affect him at all. What a good man! I do wonder, though, if he has any ulterior motives. I should find out.\\Mr. Darcy: (walks away), If it contributes to Elizabeth’s happiness, I shall do it.:nl:nlMr. Bennet: What’s this? That man is in love with my girl? I don’t think that there is anyone more worthy of her. But I shall test her and her knowledge of him to see if she truly loves him.:nl:nlMr. Bennet: Well, time to head home then."
        }}]},
        
