        {"staticObjects":[],"dynamicObjects":[{"objectId":"story_dialogue","position":{"x":140,"y":-28},"objectData":{
            "text":"(Mr. Bennet reaches his house, and enters, finding Elizabeth inside):nl:nlMr. Bennet: (Time to test her) Lizzy, have you gone mad? I thought you hated that man? He is rich for sure, but will he make you happy? Do you actually love him?:nl:nlElizabeth: Do you have any other objection than your belief of my indifference?\\Mr. Bennet: No, I don’t, but we all know that Mr. Darcy is quite an unpleasant man, (let’s see) but again this would mean nothing if you really love him.:nl:nlElizabeth: I do, I do, I really love him, it is a shame that you have not gotten to know him better.:nl:nlMr. Bennet: (there it is) Well then, both of my daughters are well set off. If any young men come for Kitty or Mary, let me know.\\(Elizabeth leaves):nl:nlMr. Bennet: Phew! What a journey, so Elizabeth truly loves Darcy, what a relief. I see that acting aloof has truly paid off. My favorite daughters are getting married. Life is truly great."
        }}]},
        
